<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Congress of Tacna</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837</span> · Also known as Pact of Tacna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pact of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tacna">Tacna</a> was the agreement of May 1837 by which delegates of the North Peruvian Republic, the South Peruvian Republic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a> defined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>–Bolivian Confederation. It made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Andrés de Santa Cruz</a> Supreme Protector for ten years, with control of foreign affairs and the army. Opposition in all three states to its centralising terms weakened the confederation before its defeat in 1839.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/congress-of-tacna.jpg" alt="Congress of Tacna" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Huhsunqu assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Peru-Bolivian_Confederation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
